B = Bank('127.', 1207, own='cte_130.jsonl')
def H(code, d, q, right, wrong, e): return B.hand(code, d, q, right, wrong, e)
H("879.d.1.A",3,"A collision-repair apprentice explains to a customer why a fender needs to be replaced rather than repaired, using plain words, and then records the decision on the work order. She is demonstrating:","effective oral and written communication with individuals in the collision repair setting",["avoiding the customer","unclear speaking","skipping documentation"],"Speak and write clearly.")
H("879.d.1.A",4,"When a customer is nervous about the cost of a repair, the best approach is to:","explain the estimate item by item and answer questions calmly",["rush the conversation","avoid the question","raise your voice"],"Clear explanation builds trust.")
H("879.d.1.B",3,"A student completes a repair order by listing panel damage, labor operations, paint codes and parts. She is using:","technical writing skills to complete collision repair and refinish orders",["slang","vague notes","random drawings"],"Precise work orders.")
H("879.d.1.B",4,"Which entry is the most useful on a collision repair order?","'Replace left front fender; refinish and blend door'",["'Fix car'","'Do body stuff'","'Paint it'"],"Specific operations.")
H("879.d.1.C",3,"A technician opens the paint manufacturer's technical data sheet to find the mixing ratio and flash time for a clear coat. She is:","locating and reading documents such as service and repair information and technical data sheets",["guessing","ignoring data","using memory only"],"Read the TDS.")
H("879.d.1.C",4,"A technical data sheet gives the technician the product's:","mixing ratios, drying times and application guidelines",["price history","color of the can","maker's address"],"TDS content.")
H("879.d.2.A",3,"A student describes how a minor dent might be pulled and filled while a heavily buckled quarter panel may need to be sectioned or replaced. She understands:","the basic types of repair procedures used in collision repair",["only one method","paint only","no repair types"],"Repair or replace.")
H("879.d.2.A",4,"A panel that has been stretched and creased beyond repair limits is typically:","replaced rather than repaired",["ignored","painted over","taped"],"Beyond repair.")
H("879.d.2.B",3,"A student outlines the steps for refinishing: cleaning, sanding, priming, applying base and clear coat, and curing. She understands:","the basic preparation, application and refinishing procedures",["only the clear coat","no steps","random steps"],"Refinish steps.")
H("879.d.2.B",4,"Which step must come before spraying primer?","sanding and cleaning the repaired area",["buffing the clear coat","applying clear","masking the wheels last"],"Prep first.")
H("879.d.2.C",3,"An estimator adds 6 body-labor hours at $55, a $210 fender and 2.5 paint hours at $60. She is:","estimating parts and labor costs on a collision repair order",["guessing","ignoring cost","avoiding math"],"Estimate parts and labor.")
H("879.d.2.C",4,"Parts of $210 plus 4 hours of labor at $50 an hour equals a total of:","$410",["$260","$210","$510"],"210 + 200 = 410.")
H("879.d.3.A",3,"A student identifies a dual-action sander, a body hammer, a dolly and a spray gun on a tool board. She is identifying:","hand and power tools and equipment commonly used in collision repair",["kitchen tools","garden tools","office tools"],"Tool ID.")
H("879.d.3.A",4,"A dolly is used with a body hammer to:","shape or smooth metal from the back side of a dent",["spray paint","grind metal","clean glass"],"Hammer-and-dolly.")
H("879.d.3.B",3,"A student identifies MIG welding and plasma cutting as common processes for joining and cutting steel panels. She is identifying:","proper welding and cutting techniques and processes used in collision repair",["a paint process","a washing method","a polishing method"],"Welding and cutting.")
H("879.d.3.B",4,"Before welding near a fuel tank, a technician should:","remove or protect fuel-related components and have a fire extinguisher ready",["weld faster","ignore sparks","skip PPE"],"Fire safety.")
H("879.d.3.C",3,"A student labels solvents, isocyanate hardeners and used filters as hazardous and uses the correct storage and disposal. She is identifying:","environmentally hazardous materials and appropriate handling and disposal",["harmless materials","trash","water"],"Haz materials.")
H("879.d.3.C",4,"Isocyanates in some automotive clear coats require a technician to wear:","a supplied-air or properly fitted respirator",["no mask","a dust mask only","sunglasses only"],"Respiratory hazard.")
H("879.d.3.D",3,"A shop teaches students about aluminum-intensive bodies, adhesive bonding and driver-assist sensors. This shows awareness of:","new and emerging collision repair and refinishing technologies",["old methods only","no change","a closed field"],"New tech.")
H("879.d.3.D",4,"After a collision, a vehicle with a camera-based driver-assist system may need:","sensor recalibration",["tire rotation","only paint","a new radio"],"ADAS calibration.")
H("879.d.4.A",3,"A student checks the cord of a sander, wears eye and hearing protection and clamps a panel before grinding. She is demonstrating:","the safe use of various hand and power tools and equipment",["careless habits","ignoring rules","unsafe practice"],"Tool safety.")
H("879.d.4.A",4,"Before using a grinder, a technician should confirm that the:","guard is in place and the wheel has no cracks",["wheel is wet","guard is removed","tool is plugged into a damaged cord"],"Check guard and wheel.")
H("879.d.4.B",3,"A student identifies mild steel, high-strength steel, aluminum and carbon fiber panels on a car and the repair method each requires. She is identifying:","types of vehicle construction materials and associated repair methods",["paint colors","tire types","radio types"],"Materials and methods.")
H("879.d.4.B",4,"High-strength steel should not be repaired with excessive heat because it can:","lose its strength",["gain strength","change color only","become lighter"],"Heat weakens HSS.")
H("879.d.4.C",3,"A technician uses a dual-action sander with 80-grit paper to remove old paint from a dented door skin. She is:","removing paint from the damaged area of a body panel",["adding paint","washing the door","painting"],"Strip the paint.")
H("879.d.4.C",4,"Stripping the paint down to bare metal around a dent before repair is done so that:","the metal can be worked and the filler adheres properly",["it looks neat","it saves sandpaper","it adds weight"],"Proper adhesion.")
H("879.d.4.D",3,"A technician runs a hand over a repaired panel with a thin glove and uses a straightedge to find low and high spots. She is:","identifying and repairing surface irregularities on a damaged body panel",["painting","ignoring dents","guessing"],"Surface checking.")
H("879.d.4.D",4,"A high spot in a panel is usually corrected by:","tapping it down with a hammer and dolly",["adding filler","adding paint","adding tape"],"Low spots take filler, high spots get tapped.")
H("879.d.4.E",3,"A technician holds a dolly behind a dent and strikes the surrounding high area with a body hammer. She is demonstrating:","hammer and dolly techniques for dent repair",["painting","grinding","welding"],"On-dolly and off-dolly.")
H("879.d.4.E",4,"Striking directly over the dolly is called:","hammer-on-dolly work, which stretches the metal",["hammer-off-dolly work","painting","masking"],"On-dolly stretches metal.")
H("879.d.4.F",3,"A technician wipes a repair area with a wax-and-grease remover, then follows with a water-based cleaner before sanding. She is:","preparing a damaged area using water-based and solvent-based cleaners",["painting","guessing","avoiding prep"],"Clean first.")
H("879.d.4.F",4,"Wiping a surface with a clean cloth in one direction rather than scrubbing back and forth helps to:","lift contaminants instead of spreading them",["add contaminants","scratch the panel","dry the cloth"],"Clean technique.")
H("879.d.4.G",3,"A technician mixes body filler with a measured amount of hardener and spreads it on a scuffed panel with a spreader. She is:","identifying, preparing and applying body filler",["painting","guessing","avoiding repair"],"Body filler.")
H("879.d.4.G",4,"Too much hardener in body filler can cause:","pinholes, staining or poor adhesion",["better curing","shrinkage","stronger repair"],"Mix by spec.")
H("879.d.4.H",3,"A technician uses a block with 80-grit to shape filler, then follows with 180 and 320 grit before primer. She is:","rough sanding body filler to contour the panel and finish sanding for the application",["painting","guessing","ignoring grit"],"Progressive sanding.")
H("879.d.4.H",4,"A guide coat is used while sanding to:","reveal high and low spots on the surface",["dry the filler","add color","clean the panel"],"Guide coat.")
H("879.d.4.I",3,"A student prepares a panel and applies a primer-surfacer, then wet sands it before color. She is demonstrating:","the proper preparation, application and refinishing of various types of primers",["washing the car","polishing","welding"],"Primer.")
H("879.d.4.I",4,"A primer-surfacer is used mainly to:","fill small scratches and give the paint a uniform base",["thin the paint","speed drying","cool the gun"],"Primer function.")
H("879.d.4.J",3,"A student keeps the spray gun perpendicular to the panel, overlaps each pass by 50 percent and holds a steady distance. She is:","applying finish using appropriate spray techniques such as gun arc, angle and overlap",["spraying randomly","painting by guess","avoiding technique"],"Spray technique.")
H("879.d.4.J",4,"Tilting the spray gun at an angle at the end of each pass can cause:","uneven thickness and streaking",["a perfect finish","better coverage","faster drying"],"Keep the gun square.")
H("879.d.4.K",3,"A student sprays two coats of basecoat, waits the flash time, and finishes with two coats of clear. She is:","applying basecoat and clear coat for overall refinishing",["washing","polishing only","sanding only"],"Base and clear.")
H("879.d.4.K",4,"The clear coat is applied over the basecoat to:","protect the color and give gloss",["remove color","fill dents","speed drying"],"Clear protects.")
H("879.d.4.L",3,"After a new finish has cured, a student wet sands a dust nib with 1500 grit and polishes the area with a buffer. She is:","sanding, buffing and polishing a finish to remove defects",["painting","welding","stripping paint"],"Defect removal.")
H("879.d.4.L",4,"Buffing a finish too aggressively on a panel edge can:","burn through the clear coat",["add gloss","fill scratches","harden the paint"],"Careful on edges.")
H("880.d.1.A",3,"An estimator explains to an insurance adjuster why a bumper cover and its reinforcement bar must both be replaced, and notes the conversation in the file. She is applying:","effective oral and written communication skills in collision repair",["poor writing","avoiding talk","unclear speech"],"Communicate with others.")
H("880.d.1.A",4,"A collision shop supervisor tells an upset customer about a delay. The most effective approach is to:","give an honest update and a revised delivery date",["blame the customer","hide the problem","stop answering calls"],"Honest updates.")
H("880.d.1.B",3,"A technician writes on the repair order which panels were repaired, replaced or refinished, plus any supplements discovered during teardown. She is using:","technical writing skills to complete collision repair orders and reports",["slang","vague notes","random drawings"],"Document supplements.")
H("880.d.1.B",4,"A supplement to an estimate is needed when:","hidden damage is found after the car is disassembled",["the customer likes the color","the car is washed","the tires are new"],"Supplemental damage.")
H("880.d.1.C",3,"A technician looks up the OEM procedure for replacing a quarter panel and the sectioning locations allowed by the manufacturer. She is:","locating, reading and interpreting service and repair information",["guessing","ignoring procedures","using memory only"],"OEM procedures.")
H("880.d.1.C",4,"A repair should follow the vehicle manufacturer's procedures because they:","preserve the vehicle's crash performance and warranty",["are optional","are cheaper","shorten paperwork"],"OEM methods.")
H("880.d.1.D",3,"An estimator multiplies 3.5 body hours by $62 per hour and adds a $145 part, then applies a 6 percent sales tax to the part. She is:","applying mathematical skills to the estimating process",["guessing","avoiding numbers","ignoring tax"],"Estimating math.")
H("880.d.1.D",4,"If labor is 4 hours at $65 and parts are $300, the total before tax is:","$560",["$365","$260","$460"],"260 + 300 = 560.")
H("880.d.2.A",3,"A student explains when a non-structural panel can be repaired with hand tools and when a section needs to be cut out and replaced. She understands:","the basic types of repair procedures for the collision repair industry",["only paint","no repair types","only welding"],"Repair types.")
H("880.d.2.A",4,"A repair is generally preferred over replacement when the damage is:","minor and within the panel's repair limits",["extreme","beyond repair","structural and kinked"],"Cost-effective repair.")
H("880.d.2.B",3,"Before repairs begin, a technician measures frame points and checks gaps and seams for hidden damage. She is performing:","a pre-repair inspection of non-structural and structural components",["a paint job","a sale","a body wash"],"Inspect first.")
H("880.d.2.B",4,"A pre-repair inspection is important because it:","finds hidden damage that affects the repair plan",["adds cost only","delays the job","avoids paperwork"],"Plan the repair.")
H("880.d.2.C",3,"A technician sands, primes and applies base and clear to a repaired door, then blends the color into the adjacent panel. She is demonstrating:","the proper preparation, application and refinishing of various finishes",["washing the car","welding the panel","stripping the paint"],"Refinish work.")
H("880.d.2.C",4,"Blending the new color into the neighboring panel is done to:","avoid a visible color mismatch",["use more paint","save clear coat","speed drying"],"Blend for match.")
H("880.d.2.D",3,"An estimator totals the labor operations and the parts on a collision job in an estimating system. She is:","estimating parts and labor costs of collision repair",["guessing","ignoring cost","avoiding math"],"Total the estimate.")
H("880.d.2.D",4,"A collision estimate typically lists parts, body labor, paint labor and:","paint materials and sublet or other charges",["driver's age","the owner's hobbies","the day's weather"],"Complete estimate.")
H("880.d.2.E",3,"A technician uses a tram gauge and a three-dimensional measuring system to compare a unibody's dimensions to the specification. She is:","performing precision measurements to diagnose vehicle body shape and frame condition",["painting","guessing","ignoring specs"],"Measure the body.")
H("880.d.2.E",4,"A unibody that measures out of specification at the strut tower indicates:","structural damage that requires pulling or replacement",["perfect alignment","a clean frame","good paint"],"Measure structure.")
H("880.d.3.A",3,"A student uses a pneumatic chisel, a body saw and a plastic welder as part of a collision repair project. She is using:","hand and power tools and equipment commonly employed in collision repair",["kitchen tools","garden tools","office tools"],"Tools of the trade.")
H("880.d.3.A",4,"A technician should inspect an air tool's hose and fittings before use to prevent:","hose whip and tool failure injuries",["tool shine","tool noise","tool weight"],"Pre-use check.")
H("880.d.3.B",3,"A student compares squeeze-type resistance spot welding with MIG plug welding for joining panels on a late-model vehicle. She is identifying:","proper welding and cutting techniques and processes in collision repair",["painting","washing","polishing"],"Welding methods.")
H("880.d.3.B",4,"Following the vehicle maker's welding procedure is important because heat can:","change the properties of high-strength materials",["improve every material","cool the panel","lighten the car"],"Heat effects.")
H("880.d.3.C",3,"A student collects used solvents, filters and paint waste in labeled containers for licensed disposal. She is:","properly handling and disposing of environmentally hazardous materials",["dumping them","ignoring rules","using drains"],"Hazmat disposal.")
H("880.d.3.C",4,"Used paint thinner should be disposed of by:","a licensed waste hauler or approved recycler",["pouring down the drain","burning","dumping on the ground"],"Regulated waste.")
H("880.d.3.D",3,"A technician studies how to repair carbon-fiber reinforced plastic parts and aluminum structures and how adhesives are used in new vehicles. She is demonstrating knowledge of:","new and emerging collision repair technologies",["old equipment","only paint","no change"],"Emerging repair tech.")
H("880.d.3.D",4,"Aluminum repair should be done in a separate area from steel repair to prevent:","cross-contamination that causes galvanic corrosion",["noise","extra paint","speed"],"Dedicated aluminum areas.")
H("880.d.4.A",3,"A technician checks the shop's fire extinguishers, spray-booth filters and eyewash station on a schedule. She is:","performing regular audits and inspections to maintain compliance with safety requirements",["ignoring safety","decorating","avoiding checks"],"Safety audit.")
H("880.d.4.A",4,"A spray-booth's airflow and filters must be checked regularly to:","protect workers from overspray and reduce fire risk",["add paint","dry the floor","reduce noise"],"Booth maintenance.")
H("880.d.4.B",3,"A student identifies a car's steel, aluminum, magnesium and composite parts and how each is repaired. She is identifying:","types of vehicle construction materials and associated repair methods",["paint types","tire types","glass types"],"Materials ID.")
H("880.d.4.B",4,"Magnesium parts in a vehicle should be repaired carefully because the metal is:","flammable when ground or heated",["too soft to touch","magnetic","water soluble"],"Fire risk.")
H("880.d.4.C",3,"A student explains that a unibody's crumple zones absorb crash energy and describes direct and indirect damage. She is identifying:","methods of collision energy management and types of damage",["paint methods","glass types","tire types"],"Crumple zones.")
H("880.d.4.C",4,"Crumple zones are designed to:","absorb crash energy by deforming progressively",["stay rigid","add weight","reduce passenger room"],"Energy absorption.")
H("880.d.4.D",3,"An estimator walks around a vehicle, measures gaps and lists damaged parts and operations in the estimating software. She is:","determining vehicle damage and preparing an estimate of repair costs",["washing the car","painting","guessing"],"Estimating.")
H("880.d.4.D",4,"Direct damage on a vehicle is damage:","at the point of impact",["at the opposite end","only to the paint","only to glass"],"Direct vs indirect.")
H("880.d.4.E",3,"A technician judges that a dented door skin can be repaired with hammer and dolly, while a creased roof panel must be replaced. She is determining:","body panel damage and the associated repair methods",["paint color","tire size","engine type"],"Repair vs replace.")
H("880.d.4.E",4,"A sharp crease that has stretched the metal beyond reasonable repair indicates the panel should be:","replaced",["ignored","painted over","taped"],"Stretched metal.")
H("880.d.4.F",3,"A technician removes the hood, hinges and fender bolts and re-hangs them, adjusting gaps with shims. She is:","inspecting, removing, replacing and aligning body components such as hoods and fenders",["painting","washing","guessing"],"Panel alignment.")
H("880.d.4.F",4,"Panel gaps are usually checked by comparing them:","to the manufacturer's specification or the opposite side",["to a coin","to the paint color","to the tire size"],"Even gaps.")
H("880.d.4.G",3,"A student identifies a single-stage, a basecoat/clearcoat and a tri-coat finish, and the refinish method for each. She is identifying:","types of vehicle finishes and associated refinish techniques",["tire types","glass types","engine types"],"Finish types.")
H("880.d.4.G",4,"A tri-coat finish needs:","a basecoat, a mid-coat and a clear coat",["a single coat","only a primer","no clear"],"Three layers.")
H("880.d.4.H",3,"A technician removes a bolted fender, cuts a welded rocker section and bonds a new panel in place using the manufacturer's procedure. She is:","inspecting, removing and replacing bolted, bonded and welded panels",["painting","washing","guessing"],"Panel types.")
H("880.d.4.H",4,"When replacing a bonded panel, the technician should:","use the specified adhesive and cure time",["use any glue","skip curing","use tape"],"Follow the adhesive spec.")
