H("880.d.4.I",4,"A seat belt that was in use during a collision should usually be:","replaced, since it may be stretched or damaged",["reused","painted","trimmed"],"Replace after crash.")
H("880.d.4.J",3,"A technician looks at a bent radiator support, damaged headlight mounts and a cracked bumper reinforcement. She is:","identifying vehicle body components and assessing them for repair or replacement",["painting","guessing","washing"],"Assess components.")
H("880.d.4.J",4,"The radiator support is part of the vehicle's:","front structure that supports the cooling components and front end parts",["rear bumper","roof","glass"],"Support structure.")
H("880.d.4.K",3,"A student welds a patch panel with a MIG welder and cuts out damaged metal with a plasma cutter. She is demonstrating:","the welding and cutting processes used in vehicle collision repair",["painting","buffing","washing"],"Weld and cut.")
H("880.d.4.K",4,"Welding on a vehicle with electronic modules requires first:","disconnecting the battery and protecting sensitive electronics",["leaving the battery connected","welding faster","ignoring modules"],"Protect electronics.")
H("880.d.4.L",3,"A technician removes the front bumper, unplugs the fog lamps and reinstalls them once the repair is complete. She is:","removing, installing and adjusting vehicle mechanical systems and electrical components",["painting","guessing","washing"],"R&I.")
H("880.d.4.L",4,"After reinstalling a headlight, the technician should:","check its operation and aim",["paint it","ignore it","leave it off"],"Verify lighting.")
H("880.d.4.M",3,"A student examines a finish with cracks like a dried lakebed and traces it to a thick application without adequate flash time. She is:","identifying and determining the cause of paint and refinishing defects",["ignoring defects","guessing","painting"],"Defect diagnosis.")
H("880.d.4.M",4,"Dust nibs in a fresh clear coat are most often caused by:","contamination in the booth or on the surface",["too much sun","low humidity","perfect cleaning"],"Cleanliness.")
